				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/aceofmoxes" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2943332); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=2943332&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607935838" alt="Aceofmoxes" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=2943332)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/aceofmoxes" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2943332); return false;" >Aceofmoxes</a></span> <span class="odate time_1487945887 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">24 Feb 2017 14:18</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2754462">
									

<p>-1. Doesn't provide interesting perspective, scientific exploration, or a story.</p>
<p>My number one gripe here is biological contamination. It's virtually impossible to prevent an unmanned probe from bringing Earth life<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-621186-1" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnote-621186-1')">1</a></sup> to other planets, even when traveling years in space. NASA considers this a huge ethical concern for Europa, but the foundation is unconcerned?</p>
<p>Related, Bringing the D-class back is more serious chance for contamination. Consider that Moon dust is hazardous<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-621186-2" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnote-621186-2')">2</a></sup> and it's basically the same stuff as in Earth. An alien disease would be a new keter SCP in its own right. The potential to bring dangerous material justifies the disposable in D-class.</p>
<p>Speaking of disposable and unmanned probes, why not use drones? A bomb-disarming robot is cheap<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-621186-3" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnote-621186-3')">3</a></sup> and nearly as useful as a D-class. This seems like a needless waste of D-classes.</p>
<p>Check out the other portal-exploration SCP for ideas. Usually, the locations are linked thematically and tell a story.</p>
<div class="footnotes-footer">
<div class="title">Footnotes</div>
<div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-621186-1"><a href="javascript:;" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnoteref-621186-1')">1</a>. or the building blocks thereof</div>
<div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-621186-2"><a href="javascript:;" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnoteref-621186-2')">2</a>. like asbestos.</div>
<div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-621186-3"><a href="javascript:;" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnoteref-621186-3')">3</a>. cheap by foundation standards at least, certainly less than a space suit</div>
</div>

							</div>

								
