<blockquote>
<p>It's virtually impossible to prevent an unmanned probe from bringing Earth life to other planets, even when traveling years in space. NASA considers this a huge ethical concern for Europa, but the foundation is unconcerned?<br />
&#8230;<br />
An alien disease would be a new keter SCP in its own right.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>To be fair, except for extremophiles, I don't think many microbes could survive in very different environmental conditions from Earth[[Footnote]]I'm aware of the bacteria found from recovered probes during the Apollo missions, but it should be noted that those <em>went into hibernation</em> in an attempt to wait for favorable conditions, if they could survive that long. [[/footnote]]. And that's assuming that the amino acids the local biosphete uses are compatible with the microbes to begin with.</p>
<p>This is all hypothetical until we encounter at leastvone alien biosphere, however, so real-world NASA has a good reason to be cautious rather than just assume.</p>

